[codespell]
skip = *.pyc,*.json,*.xml,*.lock,*.mp3,*.whl,./.venv,./.build,./.git
ignore-words-list = rouge,fo,Exting,AKS,UE,patter,Speaches,speaches,retuned,sting,summar,pres,isnt,arent,wasnt,werent,dont,doesnt,didnt,hasnt,havent,cant,couldnt,wouldnt,wont,shouldnt,canonicalizations,covert,disjointness,mot,Carin,Hart,Empress,ist,Wege
# canonicalizations: legitimate plural (a count of host-identity canonicalization steps, RFC-109); codespell false-positives -izations plurals
# covert: real word ("a covert vLLM shim" — hidden/disguised, ADR-147); not a typo of "convert"
# disjointness: real word ("vendor disjointness" — the state of being disjoint, ADR-149/JUDGING.md); not a typo
# mot: local variable name (max_output_tokens abbrev, gemini_provider.py); not a typo of "not"
# Wege: German for "paths/ways" — the p13 fixture's literal episode title
# (`Wege Bauen, Die Bleiben`), quoted in workflow/translation_stage.py as the measured
# evidence for why a title must travel with context. Quoting a non-English string is
# unavoidable in a multilingual pipeline's docs; not a typo of "Wedge".
# ist: German for "is" — a member of the `_MARKERS["de"]` function-word set in
# search/query_language.py, which detects a query's language from words that are common in
# one language and rare in English. Every list there is deliberately foreign vocabulary, so
# more of these will arrive as languages are added; not a typo of "is".
# Carin / Hart: people's names (Carin Zissis, Americas Quarterly; Emily Hart, Colombia Calling) —
# measured evidence for the remove-only feed-host rule (#2075); not a typo of "Caring"
# Empress: a real title, in the worked example for the matched-bracket rule in
# identity/slugify.py ("Empress Elisabeth (Sisi)"); not a typo of "Impress"
# fo: placeholder; rouge: metric name; Exting: transcript artifact pattern in preprocessing (literal, not typo of "Existing")
# pres: deliberate title abbreviation ("Pres"/"Gov") in the political-title token set (hosts.py); not a typo of "press"
# UE: macOS kernel uninterruptible wait process state (RFC-074)
# patter: rapid/glib speech (podcast host patter); not a typo of "pattern"
# Speaches/speaches: product name (github.com/speaches-ai/speaches — renamed faster-whisper-server), not a typo of "Speeches"
# retuned: past tense of "re-tune" (e.g. "the model was retuned with a Gemma-native prompt"); not a typo of "returned"
# sting: a real word (the musician Sting / a bee sting) — used as a mononym example in the speaker roster (#876); not a typo of "string"
# summar: intentional prefix in provider_metrics.py operation-name matching (catches "summary", "summarize", "summarization") — not a typo of "summary"
# isnt/arent/wasnt/werent/dont/doesnt/didnt/hasnt/havent: intentional patterns in
# gi/insight_type_classifier.py — apostrophe-stripped contractions that match
# transcript artifacts where the transcriber dropped the apostrophe. Not typos.
